-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  lex_splices_err_space_after_operator.pcpp - Lexical: a blank after a splice after an operator

  Break step of lex_splices: a blank after a splice's backslash right
  after an operator is one LX0201, a warning at the backslash (the
  operator is not read twice): the module builds. The marked line ends
  in the splice, so its marker is a block-comment marker.
  Its bytes are part of the test (see above): edit it with an editor
  that keeps them as they are.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe lex_splices_err_space_after_operator;

/*
  @@test
    kind build
  @@end
*/

var
  LN: int32;

begin
  LN := /* // WARN LX0201@40 // */ 1 +\ 
2;
end.
